    {
      "id": "5ef8a7b9a9066bab4b8b554e3c139494bf72c23e",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2189728514,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It looks as if:\n\n- if `gcry_md_open(&md5_handle, GCRY_MD_MD5, 0)` returns 0, all 16 octets of the hash buffer are set by an `memcpy()`;\n- otherwise, they're not set at all.\n\nAt least as I read https://www.gnupg.org/documentation/manuals/gcrypt-devel/Working-with-hash-algorithms.html, if `gcry_md_open()` returns a non-zero value, it indicates an error. If an error occurred, presumably that means that we don't have a message digest; if so, are any of the other calculations done there meaningful?\n\n(Also, presumably some instances of `162 should be replaced by `HASH_MD5_LENGTH`.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-11-01T20:13:44.525Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-11-01T20:13:44.525Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 339090081,
